Java is a object oriented language:
	class: defines object properties and actions
	inheritance: shares features between classes
	polimorphism: action adapts to objects
	encapsulation: hides sensitive details, prevents unauthorized changes

Platform independence:
	Converts java code into bytecode
	enables multiplatform utilization

Strongly typed language: 
	every variable requires declaration to catch errors during compilation
	ensures better code quality
	helps reduce bugs

Automatic memory management

Multithreading
	Allows threads to run simultaneously
	Makes apps smoother and faster

Comprehensive standard library: Includes tools for:
	Networking
	Data structures
	File handling
	handle HTTP request

Security

Versatility:
	robust webapps
	android apps
	complex systems

Latest trends in Java:
	Cloud development
	Serverless architecture (AWS)
	AI and machine learning
	Spring framework
	IDEs (IntelliJ IDEA, Eclipse, VSCode)
